{
  "id": "blazor.toggle-navigation-with-csp",
  "edition": "11.0",
  "title": "Operate navigation without an inline script exception",
  "goal": "Keep a Blazor Web App menu working under strict handler CSP.",
  "areas": [
    "blazor"
  ],
  "exampleLanguages": [
    "csharp"
  ],
  "tags": [
    "bracken-menu",
    "navigation",
    "security"
  ],
  "apis": [
    "NavMenu",
    "customElements"
  ],
  "introducedIn": "11.0",
  "supportedTargets": [
    "11.0"
  ],
  "stability": "stable",
  "applicability": {
    "routes": [
      {
        "target": "11.0",
        "usage": "primary",
        "conditional": false,
        "selectionNotes": [
          "Accepted NavMenu migration; module path differs with client layout."
        ],
        "requirements": {
          "runtime": {
            "name": ".NET",
            "version": "11.0",
            "match": "release-family",
            "reason": "Current Web App template baseline; the module migration also executes on the .NET 10 comparison. This is not a new JavaScript runtime API."
          },
          "sdk": {
            "name": ".NET SDK",
            "version": "11.0",
            "match": "release-family",
            "reason": "Use matching Web SDK, reference packs and browser assets; RC2 is the tested pin."
          },
          "language": {
            "name": "C#",
            "version": "15.0",
            "match": "exact",
            "reason": "Current canonical language mode; the module migration requires no new C# syntax."
          },
          "frameworks": [
            "ASP.NET Core 11"
          ],
          "packages": [
            {
              "name": "Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly",
              "version": "11.0",
              "match": "release-family",
              "reason": "Global client variant only; exact RC2 package is pinned in the example."
            },
            {
              "name": "Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Server",
              "version": "11.0",
              "match": "release-family",
              "reason": "Host integration for the global WebAssembly variant; not a prerequisite for static or Server-only navigation."
            }
          ],
          "workloads": [],
          "packageAssets": [
            "Collocated .razor.js modules; matching SDK browser assets"
          ],
          "providers": [],
          "platforms": [
            "Browser"
          ],
          "renderingModes": [
            "Static SSR with enhanced navigation",
            "Interactive Server",
            "Global Interactive WebAssembly"
          ],
          "prerequisites": [
            "Accepted NavMenu migration; module path differs with client layout. Retain the app document, base URI, styles, imports and endpoint setup supplied below.",
            "Without global client interactivity, use Components/Layout/NavMenu.razor.js. With a .Client project and global client interactivity, use Layout/NavMenu.razor.js. Resolve through Assets and the application base; never hard-code a fingerprint.",
            "Allow trusted external app/framework scripts. The local WebAssembly check retains wasm-unsafe-eval; the Server check retains its local circuit connection. These script/connection requirements are separate from the removed handler exception.",
            "Browser ES modules, ES2022 private class fields, custom elements, Element.closest and checkbox support; local Chrome 155 executes both paths. No database, external provider, account, resource or installed workload is needed. Required workloads: [] does not describe the host installed inventory."
          ],
          "constraints": [
            "Remove the inline handler and its matching hash together; remove unsafe-hashes only when no other required handlers use it. Do not remove unrelated script hashes/nonces or broaden the policy to unsafe-inline.",
            "The module scopes events to the component, closes only an open menu, removes its listener on disconnection and restores it on connection. Guard custom-element registration because modules may be encountered again during enhanced navigation.",
            "The .NET 10 sample fairly compares a deliberate matching-hash exception, a strict negative control and an executed external-module backport. Target 10 remains comparison-only in this edition; the catalogue retains exactly eight .NET 10 foundations.",
            "Static SSR navigation needs no interactive menu circuit. A separate live Server confirmation proves initialization; global client checks prove actual browser WebAssembly. Auto, legacy standalone Blazor hosting, other browsers, production/TLS policies and GA are not verified.",
            "The sample prefix is /bracken/. UsePathBase precedes explicit UseRouting; the document base and module requests share the prefix. Local ws://localhost:* is not a deployment prescription."
          ],
          "optIns": [],
          "stabilityLimitations": [
            "RC2 verification; GA unverified. No experimental API opt-in."
          ]
        },
        "evidenceSamples": [
          "samples/net11.0/BrackenMenu/Host/BrackenMenu.Host.csproj",
